course: dictionary
lesson: 862
title: Bicycle in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bicycle is a vehicle with two wheels that you ride by pushing pedals with your feet. People often shorten it to bike, so «bike» and «bicycle» mean the same thing.
explain: Context helps you find the meaning of a word. In «4 bicycles, 2 tricycles and 3 unicycles», the words around bicycle show it is one kind of wheeled ride, and the numbers tell you how many wheels each one has.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Two tired» in the bicycle joke sounds like «too tired», and the word bike still fits the sentence about two tyres, so the meaning holds.
fact: A bicycle is a vehicle with two wheels.
fact: You ride a bicycle by pushing its pedals with your feet.
fact: «Bicycle» is often shortened to «bike».
fact: «Tandem» is a bicycle built for two riders.
fact: «Bicycle» can also be a verb, but it is rare: people usually say «ride a bicycle».
exercise: How many wheels does a bicycle have? | One | *Two | Three | Four
exercise: What is a bike? | *Another name for a bicycle | A boat with sails | A large bus | A kind of helmet
exercise: In the sum «13 − 8 = 5 ride bicycles», what does the 5 count? | *Riders on bicycles | Tandems | Wheels | Pedals
test: In the spoonerism «a well-boiled icicle» for «a well-oiled bicycle», what gets swapped? | Two lines of a poem | Two whole sentences | *The first sounds of two words | The last letters of a sentence
test: In the bicycle joke, «two tired» sounds like «too tired» because a bike has what? | Three tyres | Four wheels | *Two tyres | No tyres
exam: Which word means the same as bicycle, as in «a bike»? | Tricycle | Vehicle | Unicycle | *Bike
